Spoilers within.



Basically the goal for me was to get very low AC.  I got it down to -116 
(including -48 from armor and -4 from a ring) before I got bored and just 
ascended.  Now I'm kicking myself for not going to -128.

Tame leprechauns and a =oC allowed me to donate essentially infinitely.  
That got my naked AC down to -10.  Tip:  arrange it so that you can see 
your leprechaun, but you can't see the priest (or shopkeeper).  Then the 
leprechaun will get in the first hit and not get demolished by 
the "victim".  Well placed boulders help with this.  If you need a robe, 
nymphs can work on the same principle.

After -10, a black pudding, ice box, and an altar gave me the rest.  (I 
wished for the ice box)
1. Kill lots of stuff and pile corpses into the refrigerator
2. Sacrifice until you no longer get four leaf clovers
3. Break a mirror and put away all luck-items, possibly including quest 
artifacts.  This prevents crowning.
4. Pray
5. Sacrifice until you feel reconiliation and immediately go to step 4.
6. When you run out of corpses, go to step 1.
7. When you run out of mirrors... well, that never happened.  :)

At one point I encountered a nurse, and I thought, oh good, some free HP.  
I strip naked.  The nurse misses.  The nurse misses.  The nurse misses.  
The nurse misses.  The nurse misses. ...  I think my HP were already too 
high anyway (from golden glows) for her to have helped, even if she had 
been able to hit me once in a while.

One final note:  avoiding crowning obviously has a big impact on how much 
sacrificing is required per point of AC.  A cursed luckstone won't help 
reduce your luck for the purposes of avoiding crowning!  The spoilers are 
not clear on this.  An exploration into the source revealed that having a 
cursed luck-item is a minor problem and will always be fixed before you get 
a pat on the head, and the odds of getting crowned are dependent on your 
luck AFTER this fix.

I tried taming the riders (as a vampire lord I drained Famine to level 0) 
but for some reason it didn't work for me.  I think maybe I didn't try 
enough times.

-Jamie


